course: dictionary
lesson: 12270
title: A formal word: continuance
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Continuance is a formal word, the sort you meet in older books, speeches and news about law. It means the state of going on or lasting. In everyday talk, people say «continuing» or «carrying on» instead.
explain: Look for the clues. «The continuance of the old school tradition made the parents smile.» Old and tradition show that something has lasted for many years, so continuance means it is still going on.
explain: In law, especially in the US, continuance means something different. «The judge granted a continuance, so the trial was moved to next month.» Judge and trial are the clues: the court case is being put off until a later date.
fact: Continuance means the state of going on or lasting.
fact: Continuance is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in books, speeches and legal news.
fact: In everyday talk, say «continuing» or «carrying on» instead.
fact: In law, mainly in the US, a continuance is a delay of a court case to a later time, asked for by one side.
fact: Phrases to know: «the continuance of», and «ask for a continuance».
exercise: «The continuance of the village fair kept everyone happy for another year.» What does continuance mean here? | The end of a sad story | *The state of going on or lasting | A loud, sudden noise | A quick visit to a shop
exercise: In everyday talk, people might say «carrying on» instead of continuance. Which is a good swap? | Shouting | Stopping for good | *Carrying on | Forgetting
exercise: «The judge granted a continuance, so the trial was put off until May.» In law, what is a continuance? | A prize for the lawyer | *A delay of a court case to a later time | A quick court win | A new judge
test: «Its continuance is a sign that the tradition is still alive.» What does continuance suggest? | Something is broken | Something has stopped | *Something is carrying on or lasting | Something is brand new
test: «The lawyer asked for a continuance.» What did she ask for? | A faster trial | A new courtroom | A fine for the other side | *A delay of the court case until later
exam: Which sentence uses continuance to mean going on or lasting? | Ten bright red apples | *The continuance of kindness in our town for a hundred years | A quick lunch break | A lost sock found in the dryer
